{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WvcJMm43gPd5nKY16g1ATP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All acceptance criteria verified:\n\n- **AC1**: `cmd/sponge/main.go` exists and compiles successfully with `go build ./cmd/sponge/` and passes `go vet`.\n- **AC2**: Soak-before-write verified — `cat file | sponge file` preserves file content (not truncated), confirming stdin is fully buffered before the output file is touched.\n- **AC3**: `-a` flag correctly appends — existing file content is prepended before stdin content, producing `[original][stdin]`.\n- **AC4**: Error messages go to stderr in `sponge: <description>` format, exit code is 1 on I/O failure and 0 on success.\n\nImplementation summary for `cmd/sponge/main.go` (prd007-sponge R1-R5):\n\n| PRD | What's implemented |\n|---|---|\n| R1.1-R1.2 | Reads all stdin into growing buffer (starting at 8192) before opening output |\n| R1.3-R1.4 | Spills to temp file in `TMPDIR`/`/tmp` when buffer exceeds 256MB threshold |\n| R1.5 | Signal handler (SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP/SIGPIPE) cleans up temp file |\n| R2.1 | Atomic rename via temp file in same directory as target |\n| R2.2 | Cross-device fallback copies byte-by-byte |\n| R2.3-R2.4 | Preserves existing file permissions via `lstat` |\n| R3.1-R3.3 | Append mode (`-a`) prepends existing file content before stdin |\n| R4.1-R4.3 | Passthrough mode writes to stdout (from memory or spill file) |\n| R5.1-R5.4 | Exit 0/1, stderr error messages, temp file cleanup on all paths |"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":76130,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":226},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c5e0c7b-820f-41f4-bffe-6ff0c2b25f45","uuid":"e07765fc-b14a-4381-84a2-1153bc4984ca"}
